{
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "business_model_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly answers the 'business models' half of the query and provides a strong grouping axis with well-distributed categories. Samples are well-grounded (venture_capital for 5AM/Accel, services_consulting for 280 Group, saas for Addepar). Classifying 23andMe as 'saas' is defensible but slightly loose (it's more a consumer product/subscription), a minor stretch."
    },
    {
      "name": "customer_segment_primary",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly addresses the 'customers' half of the query and offers a distinct segmentation axis. Consumer for 23andMe and enterprise for Addepar are sound. Labeling VC firms' segment as 'enterprise' is a reasonable inference but somewhat imposed (their customers are founders/LPs), only mildly warranted by the terse text."
    },
    {
      "name": "industry_vertical_served",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A genuine, non-redundant vertical axis useful for the query. Several samples grounded (life_sciences for 5AM, financial_services for Addepar). However 280 Group -> 'education' overreads 'training/certification' (they serve product management broadly, not education vertical), and Accel -> 'financial_services' is an invented specific where the generic founder text names no vertical; a 'not_stated' would have been more correct."
    },
    {
      "name": "value_prop_primary_mechanism",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Provides a distinct mechanism-of-value axis, useful for comparing how companies create value, and appropriately uses 'not_present' for silent rows. Sample mappings are reasonable (data_insights for 23andMe/Addepar, market_access for VC firms). Some subjectivity but generally warranted readings."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
  "source_groundedness": 0.83,
  "rationale": "All four added columns give genuine, mutually distinct axes (model, customer, vertical, value mechanism) that squarely serve the query about business models and customers; none is near-constant, redundant, or a trivial length/sentiment flag. Groundedness is generally solid with sensible categorisation and correct 'not_present' handling, but industry_vertical_served shows occasional over-specific inferences from terse text (Accel->financial_services, 280 Group->education) that the source does not clearly support, lowering the table-level groundedness slightly."
}

